cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "Uncertainty-Aware Diagnosis of Precipitation Type in AI Weather Models Using an Evidential Deep Neural Network"
abstract: >-
  Code and analysis notebooks for diagnosing and verifying surface
  precipitation type (rain, snow, ice pellets and freezing rain) from
  AI-based numerical weather prediction models (Aurora, GraphCast,
  Pangu-Weather, WXFormer and FuXi) and GFS, using an evidential deep
  neural network and the Bourgouin method, verified against mPING
  reports over the contiguous United States for the 2021-22 cold season.
authors:
  - family-names: Akor
    given-names: Stanley
    affiliation: Boise State University
repository-code: "https://github.com/stanleyakor1/ai-nwp-precipitation-type"
keywords:
  - precipitation type
  - AI weather prediction
  - evidential deep learning
  - uncertainty quantification
  - mPING
  - forecast verification
